{
  "name": "TEMP Find a client in all mailboxes (read only)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "5c5e5f80-6d8a-4492-8e63-2b454ec8ebed",
      "name": "README",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "height": 300,
        "width": 720,
        "content": "## TEMP - Find a client's messages in all 7 mailboxes (READ ONLY)\n\nSearches the 3 Gmail and 4 Outlook mailboxes the conversation automation reads for a word (default: the client's name and e-mail) and lists what each mailbox holds: count, earliest and latest date, and the earliest messages (date, from, to, subject). Used to see whether a client's FIRST e-mails exist in a mailbox we already read (then the collection loses them) or in none of them (then it is a mailbox we don't read). Reads only message headers (no bodies, no attachments), changes nothing.\n\nCurrent Config searches for Etsy conversation notices ('Etsy Conversation with') to see WHICH mailboxes receive them. For one client, set gmailQuery to e.g. 'Bonam OR ttbonam86' and outlookSearch to 'Bonam'. cutoffDate only splits the list into before/after. Delete when done."
      }
    },
